<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arwald</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 686</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arwald was the last king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isle-of-wight">Isle of Wight</a> and the last pagan king in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. In 686 Caedwalla of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a> conquered the island and killed him, and, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bede">Bede</a> records, his two young brothers were baptised and then executed. The conquest ended the island's independence and brought it into Wessex.</p></div>
